# @APP_NAME@

Native FluentQt operations monitor with a responsive shell, KPI cards, live
`LineChart`, filterable `DataGrid`, and explicit domain, application,
infrastructure, and UI boundaries.

## Build

Against a FluentQt source checkout:

```bash
cmake -S . -B build -DFLUENTQT_SOURCE_DIR=/path/to/Fluent-QT
cmake --build build --parallel
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
```

Against an installed development package, omit `FLUENTQT_SOURCE_DIR` and add
its prefix to `CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH`.

The composition root is `src/app/main.cpp`. Telemetry state stays in
`application`, data sources belong in `infrastructure`, and FluentQt widgets
stay in `ui`. Check `.fluentqt/architecture.json` before adding a new
dependency direction.

`ui/components/WorkbenchShell` owns wide/narrow shell geometry. Adapt
`ui/pages/MonitorPage` and `infrastructure/LocalTelemetryRepository` for your
own metrics, device feeds, or alert streams.

## Quality report

After the window builds successfully, emit a read-only Inspector report for
the rendered widget tree:

```bash
./build/@APP_TARGET@ --quality-report
```

The command prints versioned JSON and exits. It does not change the interface.
